P2 bidirectionality (mutation) verification log — arc #140 / #152
=================================================================

Method: for each distinct new behaviour — (1) confirm the guarding test PASSES
on the real implementation; (2) apply a COMPILING mutant that inverts/breaks the
behaviour (verified to compile via `tsc --noEmit`); (3) confirm the guarding
test now FAILS, naming the test; (4) restore and confirm green again. A mutant
that stays GREEN is a finding to investigate, not a pass.

All implementation was committed BEFORE any mutation (never `git checkout` to
restore uncommitted work). Mutants are applied by content-anchored edit and
reverted by the inverse edit (capture-then-grep by content, not by line number).

Baseline: `npm test` → 1203 passed (46 files); `npm run check` → clean.

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Behaviour 1 — TAPER GEOMETRY (D1: right half ∝ carried-onward flow)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Guard: p2-drawing.test.tsx "renders two bus-seg polygons that taper: left >
right, terminal → RIBBON_MIN".
PASS (real impl): green.
Mutant (COMPILING — `tsc --noEmit` clean; grep-confirmed
  `const rightFlow = terminal ? undefined : seg.entryFlow;`): the interior
  stretch's right half uses entryFlow, so no taper (right = left).
FAIL: `× renders two bus-seg polygons that taper …` at
  `expect(leftHalf1).toBeGreaterThan(rightHalf1)`.
Restored → green.

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Behaviour 2 — TERMINAL RULE (D1/D2: RIBBON_MIN ribbon + onward "0")
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Guard: p2-drawing.test.tsx "renders terminal onward '0', a RIBBON_MIN terminal
ribbon, and the spare card line".
PASS (real impl): green.
Mutant 2a (COMPILING; grep `const rightFlow = seg.handoffResidue;`): the
  terminal ribbon uses the surplus thickness, not RIBBON_MIN.
  FAIL at `expect(busY - pts[1]!.y).toBeCloseTo(1, 5)`.
Mutant 2b (COMPILING; grep `{formatRate(seg.handoffResidue)}` inside the
  terminal endpoint): the terminal label reads "30", not "0".
  FAIL at `expect(endpoints).not.toContain("30")`.
Both restored → green.

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Behaviour 3 — ENDPOINT LABELS + COLLISION RULES (D2)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Guards: p2-drawing.test.tsx "pushes the entry label right past a coincident
group token", "suppresses a hand-off label when a group token takes the LEFT
candidate at its x2", "drops a hand-off label on a stretch too narrow for both
glyphs (thinning)".
PASS (real impl): green.
Mutant 3a (COMPILING; grep `const entryX = seg.x1 + 3 + (entryCollision ? 0 :
  0);`): the entry never pushes past a coincident token.
  FAIL at "pushes the entry label right past a coincident group token".
Mutant 3b (COMPILING; grep `… && !narrow && !!leftTokenBlocks;`): inverts the
  left-token suppression, so the blocked hand-off "90" renders.
  FAIL at "suppresses a hand-off label when a group token takes the LEFT
  candidate at its x2".
Mutant 3c (COMPILING; grep `… + ENDPOINT_GAP_PX && false;`): endpointsCollide
  never returns true, so nothing thins.
  FAIL at "drops a hand-off label on a stretch too narrow for both glyphs".
All three restored → green.

