Behaviour 7 — JUNCTION KINDS (D7: subtraction residue-in, empty-span-safe)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Guard: layout.test.ts "labels a seam after an EMPTY-SPAN belt seam-merger (kills
segments[j-1])".
PASS (real impl): green.
Mutant (COMPILING; the REJECTED `segments[j-1].handoffResidue` derivation
  substituted for `seg.entryFlow − belt.capacity`): mislabels the seam that
  follows an empty-span belt (prior emitted segment's handoff is 0, but the real
  seam carries capacity through the empty span).
FAIL at "labels a seam after an EMPTY-SPAN belt seam-merger (kills
  segments[j-1])" — exactly the regression the counter-case exists to catch.
  (The N=13 and output-merger pins stayed green under this mutant — only the
  empty-span counter-case decides it, as designed.)
Restored → green.

